@startuml Debug Bridge Architecture

!define RECTANGLE class
!define INTERFACE interface

title RISC-V SoC Debug Bridge Architecture

' Define color scheme for debug focus
!define DEBUG_COLOR #FFB6C1
!define CPU_COLOR #FFE4B5
!define MEMORY_COLOR #E6F3FF
!define PERIPHERAL_COLOR #F0FFF0
!define INTERCONNECT_COLOR #FFE4E1
!define BRIDGE_COLOR #DDA0DD

package "RISC-V SoC Debug Infrastructure" {

  ' External Debug Interface
  rectangle "External Debug Host\n(UART/JTAG)" as debug_host #DEBUG_COLOR {
    note right : Debug host connects via\nUART or JTAG interface\nfor system debug and\ncode loading
  }

  rectangle "Debug Bridge\n(UART to AXI)" as uart_debug_bridge #DEBUG_COLOR {
    note bottom : Converts UART commands\nto AXI4-Lite transactions\nfor memory/register access
  }

  ' AXI4-Lite to AXI4 Converter (Debug Path)
  rectangle "AXI4-Lite to AXI4\nConverter" as axi_conv #BRIDGE_COLOR {
    note bottom : **Critical Debug Component**\nConverts debug AXI4-Lite\nto full AXI4 protocol\nfor system access
  }

  ' RISC-V Core with Debug Focus
  package "RISC-V Core Complex" #CPU_COLOR {
    rectangle "RISC-V Core\n(RV32IM)" as cpu_core {
      note top : CPU can be halted/\nstepped via debug interface
    }

    rectangle "D-Port Bridge\n(Data Port Bridge)" as dport_bridge #BRIDGE_COLOR {
      note bottom : **Key Debug Component**\nBridges CPU data port to AXI4\nAllows debug access to:\n• CPU registers\n• Memory locations\n• Cache control
    }

    rectangle "I-Cache\n(16KB, 2-way)" as icache #MEMORY_COLOR {
      note right : Debug can:\n• Flush cache\n• Invalidate lines\n• Monitor cache hits
    }
  }

  ' Interconnect with Debug Highlighting
  package "AXI Interconnect" #INTERCONNECT_COLOR {
    rectangle "AXI4 Arbiter\n(3-to-1)" as axi_arb {
      note bottom : **Debug Priority:**\n1. External debug (highest)\n2. CPU data access\n3. CPU instruction fetch
    }

    rectangle "AXI4-Lite Tap\n(Address Decoder)" as axi_tap {
      note bottom : Routes debug transactions\nto specific peripherals\nbased on address decode
    }

    rectangle "AXI4 Retime\nBuffer" as axi_retime {
      note bottom : Provides timing isolation\nfor debug transactions\nto external memory
    }
  }

  ' Memory and Peripherals (Debug Accessible)
  rectangle "External Memory\n(DDR/SDRAM)" as ext_memory #MEMORY_COLOR {
    note bottom : **Debug Features:**\n• Load programs\n• Read/write data\n• Memory dumps\n• Breakpoint support
  }

  package "Memory-Mapped Peripherals" #PERIPHERAL_COLOR {
    rectangle "IRQ Controller\n0x9000_0000" as irq_ctrl {
      note right : Debug access to:\n• Interrupt status\n• Enable/disable IRQs\n• Force interrupts
    }

    rectangle "Timer\n0x9100_0000" as timer {
      note right : Debug control:\n• Read counters\n• Set compare values\n• Timer control
    }

    rectangle "UART\n0x9200_0000" as uart {
      note right : Debug console:\n• Send/receive data\n• Status monitoring\n• Baud rate control
    }

    rectangle "SPI\n0x9300_0000" as spi {
      note right : Debug SPI devices:\n• Flash programming\n• Device control\n• Status monitoring
    }

    rectangle "GPIO\n0x9400_0000" as gpio {
      note right : Debug I/O:\n• Pin control\n• Status reading\n• Interrupt debugging
    }
  }
}

' Debug Data Flow (Highlighted in red)
debug_host --> uart_debug_bridge : **Debug Commands**
uart_debug_bridge --> axi_conv : **AXI4-Lite**
axi_conv --> axi_arb : **AXI4 (Debug Priority)**

' CPU Debug Interface
cpu_core <--> dport_bridge : **CPU Data Port**
dport_bridge --> axi_arb : **AXI4 (Data)**

' Instruction Cache Debug
cpu_core --> icache : **Instruction Fetch**
icache --> axi_arb : **AXI4 (Instructions)**

' Interconnect Flow
axi_arb --> axi_tap : **Arbitrated AXI4**
axi_tap --> axi_retime : **Memory Access**
axi_retime --> ext_memory : **AXI4 to Memory**

' Peripheral Debug Access
axi_tap --> irq_ctrl : **Debug Access**
axi_tap --> timer : **Debug Access**
axi_tap --> uart : **Debug Access**
axi_tap --> spi : **Debug Access**
axi_tap --> gpio : **Debug Access**

' Debug Capabilities Box
note bottom : **Debug Capabilities:**\n• **Program Loading**: Load ELF files via UART to memory\n• **CPU Control**: Start/stop/step CPU execution\n• **Memory Access**: Read/write any memory location\n• **Register Access**: CPU and peripheral register access\n• **Peripheral Control**: Configure and monitor all peripherals\n• **Cache Management**: Flush/invalidate instruction cache\n• **Interrupt Debugging**: Monitor and control interrupt flow\n• **Real-time Monitoring**: Live system state observation

' Debug Use Cases Box
note top of debug_host : **Debug Use Cases:**\n• **Bring-up**: Initial system validation\n• **Software Debug**: Program loading and execution\n• **Hardware Debug**: Register and signal monitoring\n• **Performance Analysis**: Cache hit rates, timing\n• **Failure Analysis**: Post-mortem debugging\n• **Production Test**: Automated testing via debug port

@enduml